+## 1. userasset.go
+
+```go
+const (
+    maxImageBytes = 10 * 1024 * 1024
+    maxVideoBytes = 100 * 1024 * 1024
+)
+
+// UserAsset is one validated local file that gh can upload.
+type UserAsset interface {
+    Path() string
+    getAsset() *asset
+    markdown(url string) string
+    rendersAsPlayer() bool
+}
+
+type asset struct {
+    path        string
+    info        os.FileInfo
+    alt         string
+    contentType string
+}
+
+type imageAsset struct{ asset }
+type videoAsset struct{ asset }
+```
+
+The embedded field must be unnamed and named exactly `asset`, because the tests write `&imageAsset{asset{contentType: x, alt: y}}` and `&videoAsset{asset{...}}`. `getAsset` returns a pointer to the embedded asset. `Path` returns `asset.path` exactly as it was passed in.
+
+Supported extensions, matched case-insensitively, listed in this order in the error message: png, jpg, jpeg, gif, webp, svg, mp4, mov, webm. Content types: png=image/png, jpg=image/jpeg, jpeg=image/jpeg, gif=image/gif, webp=image/webp, svg=image/svg+xml, mp4=video/mp4, mov=video/quicktime, webm=video/webm. png/jpg/jpeg/gif/webp/svg are images; mp4/mov/webm are videos.
+
+```go
+// newAsset validates a path and the alt text for it, reading metadata only.
+func newAsset(path, alt string) (UserAsset, error)
+```
+
+Checks, in exactly this order, so the messages match the tests:
+
+1. `os.Stat(path)` — follow symlinks. On error return an error whose message is `path + ": " + the underlying reason` and which satisfies `errors.Is(err, fs.ErrNotExist)`. The word `stat ` must NOT appear, so unwrap an `*fs.PathError` and wrap only its `.Err`: `fmt.Errorf("%s: %w", path, pathErr.Err)`, falling back to the raw error when it is not a PathError.
+2. `info.IsDir()` -> `fmt.Errorf("%s is a directory", path)`
+3. `!info.Mode().IsRegular()` -> `fmt.Errorf("%s is not a regular file", path)`
+4. unknown or absent extension -> `fmt.Errorf("%s is not a supported file type (supported: png, jpg, jpeg, gif, webp, svg, mp4, mov, webm)", path)`
+5. `info.Size() == 0` -> `fmt.Errorf("%s is empty", path)`
+6. size over the limit -> `fmt.Errorf("%s: images must be at most %s", path, humanLimit)` where humanLimit is `fmt.Sprintf("%.1f MB", float64(limit)/(1024*1024))`, giving "10.0 MB" for images and "100.0 MB" for videos; the noun is "images" for an image and "videos" for a video. A size exactly equal to the limit is allowed.
+7. `alt != ""` on a video -> `errors.New("cannot set alt text on video")` — note this message carries no path.
+
+Default alt text when the caller passed none:
+
+- image: the base file name with its extension removed, then every `.` replaced by a space. `shot.png` -> `shot`; `SHOT.PNG` -> `SHOT`; `Screenshot 2026-08-10 at 5.38.10 PM.png` -> `Screenshot 2026-08-10 at 5 38 10 PM`; `shot#dark.png` -> `shot#dark`.
+- video: the whole base file name including the extension, unchanged: `repro.mp4` -> `repro.mp4`. This becomes the link text when a video embed degrades to a link.
+
+`markdown(url)`:
+
+- `videoAsset` returns `url` on its own, with no markdown around it, ignoring alt, because only a bare URL renders as a player.
+- `imageAsset` returns `"![" + escaped alt + "](" + url + ")"`. Escaping, applied in this order: every backslash doubled; then `[` -> `\[`; then `]` -> `\]`; then every carriage return and every newline replaced by a single space (so a CRLF becomes two spaces). Nothing else is escaped.
+
+`rendersAsPlayer`: true for videoAsset, false for imageAsset.
