+### Commentable interface
+
+Add `RepositoryDatabaseID() int64` and `RepositoryViewerPermission() string` to the `Commentable` interface. `*api.PullRequest` and `*api.Issue` already satisfy them. Grep the repo for every other implementation of `shared.Commentable` (including any in non-test files) and make it satisfy the interface too.
+
+### CommentablePreRun
+
+Order matters, because a test asserts a flag conflict is reported before a missing file.
+
+1. First, before anything else, reject the conflicts (use `cmdutil.FlagErrorf`, and note the backticks are part of the message):
+   - `--attach` together with `--web`  -> `` `--attach` is not supported when using `--web` ``
+   - `--attach` together with `--delete-last` -> `` `--attach` is not supported when using `--delete-last` ``
+2. Then resolve the assets: `opts.Assets, err = opts.AttachFlag.UserAssets()` (guard against a nil AttachFlag), returning the error unchanged — a missing file must stop the command here, and the error must still satisfy `errors.Is(err, fs.ErrNotExist)`.
+3. Set `opts.BodyProvided = cmd.Flags().Changed("body") || cmd.Flags().Changed("body-file")`. `--body ""` clears a comment, so only the flag being present can say a body was given.
+4. `--attach` counts as body input ONLY when no other input flag was given: after counting `--body`, `--body-file`, `--web` and `--editor` as today, if that count is zero and `--attach` was passed, set `InputType` to `InputTypeInline` and count it as one. This makes `gh pr comment 1 --attach shot.png` post without prompting, while `--attach --body x --editor` still reports `specify only one of ...` and `--attach --body x` is accepted with `InputTypeInline`, and `--attach --editor` stays `InputTypeEditor`.
+
+Everything else about the function stays as it is.
+
+### CommentableRun
+
+After `RetrieveCommentable` and setting `opts.Host`, and after the `DeleteLast` early return, build the uploader when — and only when — `len(opts.Assets) > 0`:
+
+```go
+uploader, err := attachments.NewUploaderForRepo(httpClient, cfg, opts.Host, commentable.RepositoryDatabaseID(), commentable.RepositoryViewerPermission())
+```
+
+with `httpClient` from `opts.HttpClient()` and `cfg` from `opts.Config()`. This must happen BEFORE any editor or prompt runs, so a credential that cannot upload fails before the editor opens. When nothing is attached, build nothing — the `--web` path on a GitHub Enterprise Server host must stay untouched.
+
+Pass the uploader down into `createComment` and `updateComment`.
+
+#### createComment
+
+After the body is settled (editor survey, confirm survey — unchanged) and immediately before the API call:
+
+```go
+body := opts.Body
+var uploadErr error
+if uploader != nil {
+    var uploaded int
+    body, uploaded, uploadErr = uploader.UploadAndAttach(context.Background(), opts.Body, opts.Assets)
+    if uploaded == 0 && uploadErr != nil {
+        return fmt.Errorf("%w\nno comment was posted", uploadErr)
+    }
+}
+```
+
+Then post `body` (not `opts.Body`). Afterwards:
+- write failed and `uploadErr != nil` -> return an error reading `<uploadErr>\n<writeErr>`;
+- write failed and no upload error -> return the write error as today;
+- write succeeded and `uploadErr != nil` -> print the URL as today, then return `uploadErr`. An asset that reached the server cannot be deleted, so the comment must still be written and the failure still reported.
+
+#### updateComment
+
+Same shape, with two differences.
+
+First, decide the starting body. `KeepExistingBody` is set by the comment commands; when it is set, no body flag was given, and the input type is not the editor, start from the existing comment text (`lastComment.Content()`) so `--edit-last --attach shot.png` appends to the comment instead of clearing it. When a body flag WAS given (`BodyProvided`), use what was given, even when it is empty — that is how a comment is cleared. The editor path is excluded because the survey was already seeded with the existing text, so substituting again would double it.
+
+Second, the message when nothing could be written is `the comment was not changed` rather than `no comment was posted`.
